.TH PORTAGE-TUI 1 "October 2026" "portage-tui 0.1.0" "Gentoo Portage Utilities"
.SH NAME
portage-tui \- interactive terminal user interface for Gentoo Portage package and USE flag management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portage-tui
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIROOT_PATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B portage-tui
is a fast, keyboard-driven terminal user interface (TUI) written in pure Rust for inspecting and managing Gentoo Linux packages, USE flags, and system updates.
.PP
It displays the \fB@world\fR package dependency tree with collapsible nodes, parses plain-English USE flag descriptions from repository metadata, tracks flag origins (\fBmake.conf\fR, \fBpackage.use\fR, or profile defaults), manages package masks and testing keywords, allows pre-flight USE flag selection before package installation, and provides safe interactive package uninstallation via \fBemerge --depclean\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line help and keybindings summary.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.
.TP
.I ROOT_PATH
Optional path to the Portage root directory (defaults to \fB/\fR on Gentoo hosts with \fB/var/db/pkg\fR, or a mock environment for testing).
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.BR Tab ", " BackTab
Switch active pane between the package tree and the USE flags list.
.TP
.BR Up " / " k ", " Down " / " j
Move cursor selection up / down.
.TP
.BR PageUp ", " PageDown
Scroll list by one page.
.TP
.BR Home " / " g ", " End " / " G
Jump to the top or bottom of the active list.
.TP
.BR Enter " (in Tree pane)"
Expand or collapse dependencies for the selected package.
.TP
.BR l " / " h " (in Tree pane)"
Expand dependencies or collapse / jump to parent package.
.TP
.BR Space " (in USE Flags pane)"
Toggle the selected USE flag (marks flag as staged).
.TP
.BR Space " (in Tree pane)"
Switch focus to the USE flags pane.
.TP
.B [m]
Toggle package mask in \fB/etc/portage/package.mask/zz-portage-manager\fR.
.TP
.B [t]
Toggle \fB~testing\fR arch keyword in \fB/etc/portage/package.accept_keywords/zz-portage-manager\fR.
.TP
.B [s]
Save all staged changes to \fB/etc/portage/\fR.
.TP
.B [a]
Open the package installation modal. Queries the repository, checks mask status, and opens the pre-install USE flag selection modal before calling emerge.
.TP
.BR [d] " / " [x]
Open the package uninstallation modal. Executes \fBemerge --deselect\fR followed by \fBemerge --ask --depclean\fR.
.TP
.B [u]
Trigger full system synchronization and update: runs \fBsudo emaint --auto sync\fR followed by \fBsudo emerge -avuDN @world\fR.
.TP
.B /
Start live search filter on packages or USE flags.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear search filter or dismiss any open modal.
.TP
.B [q]
Quit \fBportage-tui\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/portage/package.use/zz-portage-manager
Managed per-package USE flag configuration overrides.
.TP
.I /etc/portage/package.mask/zz-portage-manager
Managed user package masks.
.TP
.I /etc/portage/package.unmask/zz-portage-manager
Managed package unmasks.
.TP
.I /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords/zz-portage-manager
Managed architecture testing keywords.
.TP
.I /var/lib/portage/world
List of explicitly installed packages in the @world set.
.TP
.I /var/db/pkg/
Installed package database (VDB).
.SH PERMISSIONS
To save configuration changes without running the entire TUI as root, add your user to the \fBportage\fR group and grant group write permissions to \fB/etc/portage\fR:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo gpasswd -a $USER portage
sudo chgrp -R portage /etc/portage
sudo chmod -R g+w /etc/portage
sudo find /etc/portage -type d -exec chmod g+s {} +
newgrp portage
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR emerge (1),
.BR portage (5),
.BR make.conf (5),
.BR emaint (1)
